Third-party notices
===================

The GPL-2.0-only license in LICENSE covers original integration code unless a
file states otherwise. It does not replace third-party licenses or grant rights
to firmware. File-level notices and original authorship remain applicable.

Linux kernel
------------
The kernel is maintained separately. Its COPYING, LICENSES, file-level SPDX
identifiers and authorship are retained. kernel/source.json records the selected
revision, upstream baseline and configuration location.

Upstream kernel: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/

Platform sources and references
-------------------------------
ROCKNIX supplies SM8750 platform patches used by this port:
https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution

OnePlus vendor sources inform board wiring and device protocols:
https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750

LineageOS provides an additional reference for erhai device configuration:
https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_oneplus_erhai

The Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro Linux project provided build and recovery design references,
sensor-stack integration experience and patches:
https://github.com/yzddmr6/xiaomipad-6pro-mainline

Graphics, audio and sensors
--------------------------
Mesa and its device-table patch retain upstream authorship and licenses;
packaging/mesa/source.json identifies the inputs, and Mesa's docs/license.rst
and file notices apply. See docs/GRAPHICS.md for the integration boundary.
Project source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa

AudioReach topology inputs are recorded in packaging/audio/source.json.
The upstream BSD license accompanies the generated audio package. A compiled
topology is not proprietary DSP firmware.
Project source: https://github.com/linux-msm/audioreach-topology

The sensor stack uses hexagonrpc, libssc and iio-sensor-proxy. Original sources,
patch notices and the source records under packaging/sensors retain their
respective licenses. A project package name does not relicense its contents.

* hexagonrpc: https://github.com/linux-msm/hexagonrpc
* libssc: https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/libssc
* iio-sensor-proxy: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/hadess/iio-sensor-proxy

Build tools and distribution packages
-------------------------------------
AOSP mkbootimg and AVB tools retain their upstream licenses. BusyBox and Ubuntu
packages retain their own copyright and licensing notices. Binary deliveries
must include the corresponding source information and materials required by
their licenses. Upstream Ubuntu images and full stock ROMs are not mirrored here.

Firmware and device data
-----------------------
Qualcomm, OnePlus and Awinic binaries are separate from the project's code
license. packaging/firmware-manifest.json records per-file provenance and hashes;
packaging/firmware/README.md records the available terms and unresolved
redistribution conditions. Provenance alone is not a redistribution license.

Factory calibration, device addresses, credentials and private keys are not
shared firmware. They must come from the user's own device or be generated for
that installation, and must not appear in public images or source history.
